do you have anything to say do you have  anything to say any any apologies at all  no words just a nod of apology after  these two police officers admitted  taking unofficial photographs of a  murder scene  pc denise jaffa and pc jamie lewis were  asked to guard the area where sisters  biba henry and nicole smallman were  found dead in bushes they'd been having  fun celebrating bibba's birthday in  friend park in north london when they  were attacked by daniel hussein  rather than protecting the crime scene  police officers jaffa and lewis left  their post to take photographs and  shared them on whatsapp  shocking details of how the police  officers behaved has now emerged pc  lewis edited one of the pictures and  superimposed his own face on the photo  with the two victims in the background  he then shared this with pc jaffa who  sent it on unsolicited to a female  officer  for the family and friends of the  murdered sisters this crime has brought  added trauma  marmina has called on the metropolitan  police to take control  if you've got a rotten piece of fruit in  a book a fruit bowl it contaminates  everything around it  so we need to drill down  and get the rot out once and for all  and if these police officers do not get  a custodial sentence it will not send  the message  you are not above the law  the convictions come a week after  criticism of the lackluster response by  the met when the sisters were reported  missing  and at a time when the forces actions  are already under intense scrutiny  commissioner christa dick under pressure  to resign said in a statement  what former pc jaffa and pc lewis chose  to do that day was utterly  unprofessional disrespectful and deeply  insensitive i know that is the view of  colleagues across the met who utterly  condemn this behavior  the police officers will be sentenced in  early december with a warning from the  judge they should expect time behind  bars charlotte lomas sky news
 

